# Meson build trees: the guest cross file and both build dirs are machine-local
build/

# Commercial discs and copyrighted firmware never enter this repository; the
# gate's own disc and programs live in tests/roms and are free to distribute.
# Anything supplied for local testing goes here instead:
#   tests/roms-local/       real discs (.gdi/.cdi/.chd) and NAOMI romsets
#   tests/firmware-local/   dc_boot.bin, dc_flash.bin, naomi.zip
tests/roms-local/
tests/firmware-local/

# Projects a bug reporter attached. They carry no copyrighted content - a
# project cites its disc by hash - but they are one person's session against
# one build, they go stale the moment a timebase changes, and tests/ is not
# otherwise ignored, so `git add -A` would sweep them in.
tests/*.chimeraProject

# ...and a belt to go with those braces. tests/roms IS tracked, because the
# programs the gate builds live there - so a disc image dropped beside them is
# one `git add -A` away from being committed, which is exactly what happened
# once. No disc format is ever tracked here; the homebrew is .elf and .bin.
#
# Redistributable content somebody else wrote goes in tests/own/ instead, where
# it is tracked deliberately and its terms are written down (tests/own/README.md
# and the addendum in LICENSE). That is where the 240p Test Suite's .cdi lives.
tests/roms/*.chd
tests/roms/*.gdi
tests/roms/*.cdi
tests/roms/*.cue
tests/roms/*.iso
tests/roms/*.zip

# the sandbox writes this when a guest faults
minibox-diag.log

# The gate writes its logs, dumps and configs here; all of it is regenerable by
# running the gate, and none of it is a fixture.
waterbox/tests/work/
